.TH CLOSE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
close \- close a file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int close(int " descriptor ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR close ()
closes
.I descriptor
using the Linux x86\-64 close system call.
The wrapper does not retry an interrupted call.
Do not blindly retry a failed close: Linux may already have released the
descriptor and reused its number.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero is returned on success.
On failure, \-1 is returned and
.B errno
is set to the positive Linux error number.
Successful calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.B <errno.h>
to inspect
.BR errno .
Possible errors include
.BR EBADF ,
.BR EINTR ,
and
.BR EIO ;
other Linux
.BR close (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
This Crunch library function is linked from
.BR libcrunch.a .
Its
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR read (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch),
.BR close (2)
